From 2b793793e9bcf17eed4bc6c288d572933de75797 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:48:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Consume native token-id dtypes and strides in score kernels

Upstream-base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, candidate-38 source 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4, then selected-logit source c88a692e989c391d2c8478f0f7c2069d21d6f25b.

Rationale: remove repeated int64 casts and contiguous materializations around token-score and top-k calls. Their consumers read native int32/int64 ids, row/column strides and strided masks. Prompt ids no longer widen before scoring; top-k writes its int64 result directly from either sampled-id type.

Quality: preserve FP32 score arithmetic, token values, ordering, ranks and serialized Python ids. A zero-top-k result retains its native id view; top-k results remain int64. No model precision change.

Tests: extend native-id and layout comparisons, FP64 score checks, graph and prompt paths, wire conversion, and cold-cache preparation. Deployment experiment records two-boot GPU, allocation, profiling and timing evidence.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
